  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\u2016f(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9 & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\sqrt{t}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+2\\sqrt{t}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{4t\\sqrt{t}}{3}+t)|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{32}{3}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{68}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\u2016f(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\\frac{68}{3}}.\n$$",
